        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Map &amp; Level Editor</strong><br>Create your own maps.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customizable Game Rules</strong><br>Adjust team settings and gameplay parameters to create unique game modes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Programmable Python AI</strong><br>Write your own AI players in Python. (I recommend joining the discord for more info) </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Replay System</strong><br>Review past battles to analyze strategies and improve your tactics.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NOTE: to play your own maps you either need to setup your own dedicated server with the map(s) or contact me on Discord/Reddit to upload the map to the website (I am currently working on a way to let players upload the maps to the website) </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Steam Deck Users</strong>, please apply the following compatibility settings:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Open <strong>Properties</strong> &gt; <strong>Compatibility</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Check <strong>&quot;Force the use of a specific Steam Play compatibility tool.&quot;</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Select <strong>&quot;Steam Linux Runtime 1.0 (scout)&quot;</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Set the in-game resolution to <strong>1920x1080</strong>.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Map &amp; Level Editor</strong><br>Create your own maps.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customizable Game Rules</strong><br>Adjust team settings and gameplay parameters to create unique game modes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Programmable Python AI</strong><br>Write your own AI players in Python. (I recommend joining the discord for more info) </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Replay System</strong><br>Review past battles to analyze strategies and improve your tactics.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NOTE: to play your own maps you either need to setup your own dedicated server with the map(s) or contact me on Discord/Reddit to upload the map to the website (I am currently working on a way to let players upload the maps to the website) </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Steam Deck Users</strong>, please apply the following compatibility settings:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Open <strong>Properties</strong> &gt; <strong>Compatibility</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Check <strong>&quot;Force the use of a specific Steam Play compatibility tool.&quot;</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Select <strong>&quot;Steam Linux Runtime 1.0 (scout)&quot;</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Set the in-game resolution to <strong>1920x1080</strong>.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
